% SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
% expect-output: true
% expect-output: 4
% expect-output: -166
% Scenario: a resident face's FontBBox is executable. A Type 1 font
% program defines FontBBox as a procedure of four numbers, and setup
% code that re-encodes a font executes the name after begin and
% rebuilds the array with astore; the resident faces present it the
% same way. The reference's own outlines carry other numbers, so its
% output differs.
% Expect: true, 4, -166.
/Helvetica findfont /FontBBox get xcheck =
/Helvetica findfont begin FontBBox 4 array astore end
dup length = 0 get =
